  "id": "Compound::DB00761 - Gene::6557",
  "verbalization": "Potassium Chloride (KCl) is shown to interact with multiple members of the Slc12 family of transporters, including Slc12a1, through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that KCl binds to Slc12a7 and Slc12a6, which are involved in cation-coupled chloride cotransport, and also binds to Slc12a2, which is associated with sodium-potassium-chloride symport activity. These interactions are supported by high scores in the network, indicating a strong and consistent relationship between KCl and the Slc12 family members. The shared involvement of these transporters in chloride transport suggests that KCl may modulate their activity, potentially influencing the transport of chloride ions across cellular membranes. The presence of multiple binding sites and the involvement of these transporters in similar physiological processes support the hypothesis that KCl exerts its effects through a mechanism involving the Slc12 family of transporters. The integrated evidence highlights a plausible pathway where KCl interacts with these transporters, modulating their function and thereby affecting chloride transport.",
